{
    "pageid": 64,
    "title": "Prestige",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Prestige is one of the three main currencies in Crusader Kings II . The others are gold and piety . All can be earned and spent."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Prestige can be seen as a measure of reputation and reknown of a character or dynasty ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Along with Piety , Prestige are added to score upon death."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Effects of prestige",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Prestige, along with piety , are added to score upon death.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "+1 opinion bonus from most characters for every 200 prestige, for a maximum of +10 at 2000 prestige. (Theocratic rulers care about piety instead.)",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Nomadic khans' and khagans' opinion of each other is greatly affected by prestige, as prestige affects clan sentiment . More importantly, the increase to clan sentiment from prestige has no cap. (But, opinion boost from clan sentiment is capped at +100.)",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Determines heir under some succession laws:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Open Elective (along with age)",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Patrician Elective (along with age and funding)",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Nomadic Succession",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Imperial elective (along with certain attributes); electors' influence also affected by prestige",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some important decisions require a minimum prestige without spending it, such as:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Creating custom titles requires 1000 prestige for a kingdom and 8000 prestige for an empire.",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Prepared Invasion requires 1000 prestige",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Increasing prestige",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Monthly gain:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Held titles and direct vassal titles",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some council positions: chancellor, marshal, or steward",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Most honorary titles , along with automatic minor titles such as ruler consort",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Muslims also gain monthly prestige based on the titles of landed relatives",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Nomads also gain monthly prestige if their capital is on a holy site (of any religion)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Tribal rulers can gain monthly prestige by assigning their steward to Build Legend.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Patricians get 1 Prestige per month for every 2000 gold they have (caps out at 6000 gold ).",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Dynasty controls holy order",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some traits: Proud , Scarred , Born in the purple , Augustus , Kshatriya , Shaivist , Viking and its upgrades, Renowned Physician",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Small monthly gain from Diplomacy skill",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Concubines below age 45 or extra wives (with 4 spouses, kings and emperors following Islam or reformed pagan faiths with the Polygamy doctrine cannot earn more prestige, but only prevent prestige loss for not having 4 spouses.)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some Hospital buildings",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Lump sum gain:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Creating or usurping titles",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "As a commander , one point of prestige per 100 enemy troops slaughtered",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "As an army owner, one point of prestige per 200 enemy troops slaughtered",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Winning a war, or having contributed to a war won by your side",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Tributary wars give extra prestige",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Marriage prestige effects , when marrying into a prestigious dynasty or higher rank (not applicable if both groom and bride are Muslims)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Taking a concubine of noble birth (+25 prestige per rank of parent)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Fleet returning to port with loot from raiding",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Child tutoring events",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Various events from Hermetic Society, Warrior Lodges, War Focus, Hunting Focus, etc...",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Search for a Smith events",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The amount of prestige gained by creating, usurping or destroying a title, as well as the monthly gains from holding a title, are given in the following table:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "Name",
                            "Creation",
                            "Destruction",
                            "Usurp",
                            "Hold directly",
                            "Vassal holds"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Barony",
                            "50",
                            "N/A",
                            "N/A",
                            "0.025",
                            "0.025"
                        ],
                        [
                            "County",
                            "N/A",
                            "N/A",
                            "N/A",
                            "0.1",
                            "0.1"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Duchy",
                            "200",
                            "-200",
                            "50",
                            "0.2",
                            "0.2"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Kingdom",
                            "400",
                            "-400",
                            "100",
                            "0.8",
                            "0.8"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Empire",
                            "800",
                            "-800",
                            "200",
                            "1.6",
                            "N/A"
                        ]
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Spending prestige",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "The construction of buildings in tribal holdings costs prestige",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some nomadic horde troops require prestige to hire and maintain.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Tribal rulers can utilise tribal-exclusive retinues which cost prestige.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Some powerful CBs cost prestige, such as Tribal Invasion and Nomad Invasion",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Decisions to convert religion/culture",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "If your succession law is not Gavelkind or Elective Gavelkind, you get a prestige penalty for having unlanded sons . Exceptions are government types with only one succession law, namely:",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Muslims",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Patricians in merchant republics",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Imperial Elective",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Nomads",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Dynasty Prestige",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Dynasty Prestige is a measure of the accomplishments of an entire dynasty. It is visible by going to the dynasty screen from the character window. At birth, a character's personal prestige is set to 1/5 of their dynasty prestige. At marriage, characters gain 1/10 of their spouse's dynasty prestige (making AI more willing to marry into prestigious dynasties).  Both of those fractions are alterable in defines.lua"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Dynasty prestige is calculated by summing up all titles held by living dynasty members plus those held by deceased ones. The same title will count multiple times if held by several dynasty members in succession, so if A holds a kingdom and his son B later inherits it, the dynasty will be credited with two held kingdoms and 40 prestige. The amount of prestige per title is:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "Barony",
                            "County",
                            "Duchy",
                            "Kingdom",
                            "Empire"
                        ],
                        [
                            "1",
                            "5",
                            "10",
                            "20",
                            "40"
                        ]
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Strategies for increasing dynasty prestige",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Put your dynasty members in power: see Advanced marriage guide",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Elect your dynasty members as pope : see Papal succession#Strategies",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Arrange for extra members of your dynasty to rule theocracies or minor republics",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Especially useful for bastards because these government types disallow or discourage ruler marriage",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Grant title, investiture , or matrilineal marriage into the court of a ruler who uses Open elective succession",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Establish a vassal merchant republic with a kinsman as doge",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Give the doge a large demesne to maintain power, and to increase dynasty prestige per patrician even when not doge",
                                    "children": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "text": "Help the doge reach king tier, e.g. by granting the duchy of Venice and one additional duchy",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Accept the short reigns typical of Seniority succession, or elect old relatives with Feudal elective succession",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "See also",
            "level": 2,
